{
 "_doc": "One entry per composition. Each renders once per theme (light and dark ground). `file` is a path under capture/, or {light, dark} to pick a capture per ground. Frames: browser, mac, monitor, phone, card. Coordinates are CSS px on the canvas; rotate is clamped to 3 degrees; persp is a rotateY in degrees. `aspect` is the screen w/h (default 16:10). `pos` is object-position for the cover crop. `safeTop` pads a phone capture that came without an iOS status bar, in `safeColor`, and `statusbar` draws one (light or dark glyphs). `zoom` scales the capture inside the screen (1.45 = 145% width, anchored top-left) so a cropped window shows a region large. `ui` picks the browser chrome tone (light|dark). `screenH` sets the browser screen height explicitly, cropping the page from the top so anything below the line (here, listing photos of identifiable people) stays out of frame.",
